    "answer": {
      "short": "Finding $27\\%$ of an amount uses the multiplier $0.27$. A $73\\%$ decrease leaves $100\\%-73\\%=27\\%$ of the original, so it uses the same multiplier.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}27\\%&=27\\div100\\\\&=0.27\\\\100\\%-73\\%&=27\\%\\end{align*}$$\nA $73\\%$ decrease leaves $27\\%$ of the original, so both calculations multiply the original amount by $0.27$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
